    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0237" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4824: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-01">December 1,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received December 1—3:56 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8384. The Biddle mission<anchor n="9" xml:id="d197-f1"/> is beginning to receive
                    from the British copies of British communications addressed to certain of the
                    Governments in Exile asking their adherence to the proposed joint declaration to
                    neutrals regarding repatriation of refugees. The Department has not made it
                    entirely clear to us whether the approach is to be made by the British solely.
                    The Biddle mission has expressed to us the <pb facs="0238" n="228"
                        xml:id="pg228"/> view that the reception by the Governments in Exile might
                    be somewhat better if a parallel approach is made by the American
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="9" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>Anthony J. Drexel Biddle, Jr., was accredited near the Governments of Belgium,
                    Czechoslovakia, the Netherlands, Norway, and Poland, established in England, and
                    Yugoslavia, established in Egypt.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
